{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/982910-2e-innocents-children-in-cod","id":982910,"title":"[2E] Innocents - Children in CoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-06T13:59:16-07:00","id":982910,"title":"[2E] Innocents - Children in CoD","content":"So I prepare some one-shot for my RPG club and would want to add at least one child character to the game. And I mean real child, not '16 year old teenager that makes her own mind, thank you sir!' I got as PCs couple of years from players - but classical, elementary school child character. As I know, 1E <b>WoD: Innocents </b>had special re-scale of Attributes and Skills for child characters, but I probably would not want to mixed rules as much.<br /> <br /> <b>I think that some simple Condition or two should be enough to emulate disproportions with stats between children and teenagers/adults characters. </b>Any one have idea on those mechanical differences?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:25:00-07:00","id":982929,"title":"","content":"I <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961810-child-characters-in-regular-cofd#post961810\">posted on this exact thing</a> a while back, and the general consensus was that a Condition was the most appropriate way to handle it. Several similar but different Conditions were suggested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T21:21:15-07:00","id":983133,"title":"","content":"Now I think that we need to mix up Char's Conditions with those of Reinghell's for best chold or teen experiance. Will dwell into it in free time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-20T08:52:44-08:00","id":1005718,"title":"","content":"Returning to topic with my straight forward compilation of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> ideas. I added only Attributes cap on <i>Child</i> Condition, but still think that maybe using general -1 penalty to all actions based on Attributes past 3, maybe?<br /> <br /> General idea is that young child ( 7-12ish ) would begin with <i>Child</i>, while a young adult (17-20ish) would start with <i>Adolescent</i>. A Teenager (13-16ish) would get the worst of both worlds and start with both Conditions.<br /> <br /> <b>Child (Persistent)</b><br /> Your character is a pre-adolescent (typically between 7-12 years of age). Character at this stage of development have several disadvantages when compared to an adult; their base size is 4, their Speed factor is 4, and any unarmed attack made against an adult or adult sized creature suffers a -2 penalty. You cannot raise any of her Attributes and Skills above 3 dots. Additionally, you do not benefit from the 10-again quality on teamwork actions that involve adult characters, and adult characters gain the 8-again quality on Contested actions against her. However, the characters smaller stature works to their advantage in some situations; against adults they gain a +1 die bonus to Stealth, Breaking Free of Grapple, or when Dodging.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> When your character reaches physical maturity.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> When the characters youth causes a significant social or physical set back (especially when dealing with adults).<br /> <br /> <b>Adolescent (Persistent)</b><br /> Your character is in an awkward transitionary phase of development - no longer a child, but not yet an adult, she struggles to find her place in the world. Adults tend to assume the worst in your character until she proves her maturity to them. You begin all Social Maneuvering attempts with adult characters at a Hostile impression.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> You face prejudice or discrimination as a result of your age.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Your character reaches developmental maturity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T10:18:33-08:00","id":1007308,"title":"","content":"I thinking about adding to Child Condition effect that adults have +1 bonus on Contested rolls. It would translate nicely that Skill 3 dot Child would still have a more limited knowledge than Skill 3 dot adult on the same topic. What do you think about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T19:05:12-08:00","id":1008371,"title":"","content":"Possibly add the social disadvantage to the Child condition as well. My thinking being that 10 year-olds out at night on their own raise a lot of eyebrows .. especially among law enforcement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}